Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (tuple of ints used as kernel size must have length 2)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 6 (index tensor (v_3) is within the input tensor along the specified dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ shape(v_1, v_2) - 1
>>
Rule 9 (tensor must not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 10 (tensor must have valid dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ ndim(v_1) ≤ 4
>>
Rule 13 (tensor should not be zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) ≠ 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) ≠ 0
